# =============================================================================
#  SimpleShop.Api.http  —  ready-made HTTP requests to try the API
# =============================================================================
#  How to use:
#   • Visual Studio 2022+ / Rider: open this file → click "Send request" / ▶ above a request
#   • VS Code: install the "REST Client" extension → click "Send Request"
#  The app must be running first (dotnet run).
#  Requests are separated by lines starting with ###
# =============================================================================

@baseUrl = http://localhost:5080

### 1. Health check (the Minimal API endpoint in Program.cs) → 200
GET {{baseUrl}}/

### 2. Get ALL products → 200 + JSON array
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/products

### 3. Search products by name (query string) → 200
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/products?search=mouse

### 4. Get ONE product by id (route parameter) → 200
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/products/1

### 5. Get a product that doesn't exist → 404 Not Found
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/products/999

### 6. Create a product → 201 Created (look at the "Location" header!)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/products
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "USB-C Cable",
  "description": "1 meter, fast charging",
  "price": 9.99,
  "stock": 100
}

### 7. Create with INVALID data → 400 Bad Request (automatic validation)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/products
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "X",
  "price": -5,
  "stock": 99999
}

### 8. Create with a name that already exists → 409 Conflict (business rule)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/products
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "wireless mouse",
  "price": 19.99,
  "stock": 5
}

### 9. Update a product (replace all fields) → 200
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/products/1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Wireless Mouse Pro",
  "description": "Now with a rechargeable battery",
  "price": 34.99,
  "stock": 40
}

### 10. Delete a product → 204 No Content (run it twice: the 2nd time → 404)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/products/3
